# Defect d-lane-blocking-small2-2 (2026-11-25): two `path` entries naming one
# folder, one through a link to it, were read as two packages at exit 0 and
# both compiled, where a program holds each package under one name (panel
# 235's R3); the reader compared their spellings, and refused only two that
# fold alike. A folder is now one package by what it is on its device, so the
# catalogue does not read and the `use` that reaches through it is refused.
use <json>/parse  #~ catalogue_refused

function main()
    print(parse.x().to_str())
